king about the Kuroba brothers earlier, making me homesick. [1234] Suddenly, I sneezed loudly, startling everyone. It seems that I had caught a cold from wearing a thin shirt for a long time as a model. [1235] Koyuki seemed to notice this and apologized, \"I'm sorry! It's already November, and I've been making you wear clothes from the end of September. That's probably why you caught a cold. Take a break tomorrow!\" [1236] \"Makoto, go take a bath and warm up your body first. I'll clean up.\" Kikun says. [1237] Although I refuse, I still follow her advice. Since I'm staying with someone else, I can't even politely decline without their permission. It seems that I really miss the life outside the village\u2026from about ten hours ago. [1238] \"I'll be going now.\" I say goodbye to everyone and decide to go take a bath first. The clock on the wall shows it's around nine o'clock. This mansion has only slippers in the bathroom, and only takes them off when bathing and sleeping; but if you consider it purely as a Western-style, you'll find that the bathroom is undeniably Japanese. Perhaps because the late Mr. Shima was able to accept wearing shoes indoors but couldn't bear the Western-style bathtub. [1239] \"Wow!\" I sink my body into the cypress-scented bathtub and try to make a sound from the water. I've felt that this bathroom makes me feel very distant ever since I came here, probably because I always worry about why I'm in such a remote place, in a house full of strangers, bathing in water that someone else has already used. But now, I'm humming and leisurely soaking in the bath. [1240] \"Humans are just such animals\u2026\"\n[1241] Talking to myself in the bathroom was a habit I had since I was a child. I submerged my body up to my shoulders in the water, and my body slowly warmed up. I murmured \"comfortable\" in my mouth. After getting out of the bath, I carefully washed my hair twice. I wiped the foggy mirror clean with force and saw that the reflection in the m